---
import SiteLayout from "../layouts/SiteLayout.astro";
---

<SiteLayout
  title="Terms of service — Milton"
  description="Milton is operated by Zone of Danger, LLC. By using Milton you agree to these terms."
  legal
>
  <h1>Terms of service</h1>
  <p class="updated">
    Last updated: <time datetime="2026-11-11">November 11, 2026</time>
  </p>
  <p>
    Milton is operated by Zone of Danger, LLC. By using Milton you agree to
    these terms.
  </p>

  <h2>The service</h2>
  <p>Milton is provided as is, without warranties of any kind.</p>

  <h2>Trial and subscription</h2>
  <p>
    A new Milton account starts with a 30-day free trial. No credit card is
    required. If you delete your account and sign up again with the same
    sign-in, the new account gets no trial.
  </p>
  <p>
    After the trial, Milton costs $5.01 USD a month, billed through Stripe. To
    continue, add a card before the trial ends; you are charged when it ends and
    then every month until you cancel. If no card has been added when the trial
    ends, nothing is charged, and AI reads and saves pause until you subscribe.
    Your cover sheet, memos and tweaks stay in the Milton app to view and
    download.
  </p>
  <p>
    If a renewal payment fails, Stripe retries it. AI reads and saves continue
    for 3 days after the renewal date, then pause until the payment succeeds. If
    every retry fails, your subscription is canceled.
  </p>
  <p>
    You can cancel at any time in Stripe’s billing portal, which you open from
    the account menu in the Milton app. Cancellation takes effect at the end of
    the current billing period. Payments are not refunded, including for a
    partial month, except where the law requires a refund.
  </p>
  <p>
    Deleting your account deletes your Stripe customer record, which ends any
    subscription immediately, with no refund. Stripe keeps past invoices and
    payment records.
  </p>

  <h2>Your content</h2>
  <p>
    Your memos and cover sheet are yours. You let us store them and serve them
    to the AIs you connect, only to run Milton. We do not sell them or use them
    to train AI models.
  </p>
  <p>
    A memo is writing you accepted with an AI: its first draft, your final,
    tweaks and a one-line context summary, stored exactly as your AI sent it,
    including any names in it. It is kept until you forget it, delete all memos
    or delete your account. You are responsible for what you and your AI save.
    Every AI you connect can read your cover sheet and your memos' finals and
    tweaks and the short quotes behind them, and what it does with them is
    governed by its provider's terms, not ours. You can forget a memo or delete
    all memos, and delete your account, yourself in the Milton app.
  </p>

  <h2>Fair use</h2>
  <p>
    Stay within Milton's usage limits; do not misuse, attack or try to access
    other people's data.
  </p>

  <h2>Changes and ending</h2>
  <p>
    We may change or end the service and will give notice where we can. You can
    stop using Milton at any time and delete your account in the Milton app, or
    ask us to delete it.
  </p>

  <h2>Liability</h2>
  <p>
    To the extent the law allows, Zone of Danger, LLC is not liable for indirect
    or consequential losses, and our total liability is limited to the amount
    you paid us.
  </p>

  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p>
    <a href="mailto:support@meetmilton.com">support@meetmilton.com</a>.
  </p>
</SiteLayout>
